deploy_gate:
  instruction: Before deploying TinyRustLM.MiRust.com or TinyRustLM.com, update this developer portal, MiRust.com, MiniModel.org, and any remaining SLMComposer.com redirect/public export surfaces to match the deployed source behavior.
  requirements:
    - Keep source options, .slm verification claims, model documentation, and no-server-model-byte boundaries current.
    - Document Hugging Face metadata/conversion handoffs, Rust conversion receipt MiniModel command hints, shared simple/advanced source-row actions, MiniModel `prepare-peer-share` sender packages, generated local `.minimodel-serve-peer-pieces.ps1` sender helpers, MiniModel `serve-peer-companion` state+piece serving including path-prefixed peer base URLs, MiniModel `add-peer-source` late peer-source publication, MiniModel `write-peer-source-announcement` portable availability metadata, `write-peer-source-announcement-feed` availability feeds, `inspect-peer-source-announcement-feed` local feed preflight, feed-bound `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcement-feed` snapshots, MiniModel `inspect-catalog-snapshot` local catalog snapshot preflight, MiniModel `write-peer-companion-state` local companion handoff metadata plus `inspect-peer-companion-state` validation, MiniModel `write-peer-contact-card` / `inspect-peer-contact-card` known-peer URL handoff metadata, generated `converted-once-p2p-publish.README.txt`, same-origin checksum-bound catalog announcement feed routes including strict feed-envelope validation and valid empty feeds, MiniModel `apply-peer-source-announcements` maintainer drift checks for peer-offer route/checksum/chunk-count/Merkle identity, MiniModel `write-catalog-snapshot-with-announcements` batch metadata publication, MiniModel `write-catalog-snapshot` metadata reuse, local `models.v0.json` loading, catalog-listed MiniModel peer sources, self-locating `.minimodel-peer-import.ps1` receiver scripts, structured peer-import metadata routes and receiver validation gates, peer-import receipts with transfer evidence, and known-peer MiniModel serve/fetch handoffs with receiver-side advertised companion-state validation when TinyRustLM app behavior changes; do not imply broad P2P discovery, relays, or project-hosted model bytes until implemented.
    - Keep TinyRustLM.com documented as the root app route; do not describe /app/ as the canonical TinyRustLM.com path.
    - Keep the former standalone runtime documentation lane documented only as retired/preserved content under /docs/runtime-portal/.
    - Keep SLMComposer.com documented only as a retired or redirecting app identity, not the canonical public app.
    - Run relevant pointer audits and git diff --check before packaging or deployment.
