current_state:
  - TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the TinyRustLM developer portal.
  - TinyRustLM.com is the root-domain browser-local Rust/WASM app route.
  - Developer docs now track the protected TinyRustLM NuGet SDK distribution in SLMComposer.com: `TinyRustLM.Abstractions`, `TinyRustLM.Core`, and `TinyRustLM.P2P` expose only `.slm` validation/inspection, native-backed runtime harness operations, metadata-bound P2P share/import workflows with local manifest-piece verification, `.slm` assembly, typed announcement/catalog application and inspection, announcement JSON handoff helpers, receipt sidecars, receipt-sidecar inspection, and .NET wrappers, while conversion, quantization authoring, adapter/selector/breeding/premium/telemetry/licensing/private training internals remain outside packages. `eng/get-package-version.ps1`/`.sh` derive package version from `dotnet/Directory.Build.props` for verification, publish-set validation, and feed smokes. `eng/verify-package.ps1` and `eng/verify-package.sh` include package private-surface/source/debug/generated-output/local-path leakage inspection, a clean temporary consumer install smoke from the produced packages, and `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-package-audit.json` with package SHA-256/native RID/required metadata/XML docs/dependency/private-surface/source-debug-generated-output/local-path evidence via matching `eng/write-package-audit.ps1`/`.sh` schemas; `eng/publish-nuget.ps1`/`.sh` validate exactly the three source-versioned protected packages, reject stale or unintended extra `TinyRustLM*.nupkg` files, require package names/hashes/sizes to match the package-audit report, write `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-publish-plan.json` with audit-match evidence, record redacted `push_failed` evidence when authenticated publish fails, and support dry-run audits before private-feed or NuGet.org pushes; `eng/audit-nuget-release-readiness.ps1`/`.sh` write `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-release-readiness.json` with local gate status, target-feed status, blockers, next actions, auth mode, and non-secret API-key/Trusted-Publishing evidence; `eng/verify-feed.ps1` writes `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-feed-smoke.json` while proving clean consumer install/runtime/P2P smoke from a configured feed, and `eng/verify-feed.sh` records missing `dotnet` or other consumer-smoke failures in the same report schema; `release-nuget.yml` supports scoped API-key publishing and NuGet.org Trusted Publishing through GitHub OIDC, builds and requires `win-x64`, `linux-x64`, `osx-x64`, and `osx-arm64` native bridge assets in `TinyRustLM.Core`, runs readiness audit with blocked-state failure before push, skips package push when readiness is already `published_current`, validates the publish-plan schema after push or readiness dry-run, always runs feed-current and feed package-hash verification with short feed-indexing retries, and leaves the heavier clean consumer smoke optional; `nuget-feed-monitor.yml` runs current-version feed checks manually or daily once `TINYRUSTLM_NUGET_MONITOR_ENABLED=true`, can run clean consumer smoke when `TINYRUSTLM_NUGET_MONITOR_VERIFY_CONSUMER=true`, and can run retained-publish-plan package-byte checks when `TINYRUSTLM_NUGET_MONITOR_VERIFY_HASHES=true` with `TINYRUSTLM_NUGET_MONITOR_PUBLISH_PLAN_REPORT`; `eng/verify-feed-current.ps1`/`.sh` write `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-feed-current.json` proving the feed exposes the source-declared version and the source tree is not behind the latest feed version; `eng/verify-feed-package-hashes.ps1`/`.sh` write `artifacts/reports/tinyrustlm-nuget-feed-hashes.json` proving feed package bytes match the audited publish plan.
  - NuGet SDK wrapper update on 2026-07-06: `TinyRustLmRuntimeFactory.GetVersion()` exposes the native SDK/ABI version report, `TinyRustLmP2PClient.PrepareLocalShareKit` now returns typed `P2PShareKitReport`, `ExportShareMetadata` returns typed `P2PShareMetadata`, `ValidateAnnouncement` / `ApplyReceivedAnnouncement` return typed `P2PAnnouncement` / `P2PAnnouncementCatalog` records, `InspectAnnouncementCatalog` returns typed `P2PAnnouncementCatalogInspection`, and explicit `PrepareLocalShareKitJson` / `ExportShareMetadataJson` / `ValidateAnnouncementJson` / `ApplyReceivedAnnouncementJson` / `InspectAnnouncementCatalogJson` methods preserve exact native JSON handoff documents; clean consumer smoke now validates those typed reports and boundary flags.
  - NuGet generation-option validation on 2026-07-06: the .NET wrapper and native public runtime SDK reject invalid generation options before runtime mutation. .NET rejects non-positive `MaxNewTokens`, non-finite or negative `Temperature`, `TopK` outside `1..1024`, and non-finite/out-of-range `TopP` before P/Invoke; direct native callers receive `invalid_generation_options` before runtime-handle lookup or lossy floating-point casts.
  - NuGet managed string NUL validation on 2026-07-06: the .NET wrapper rejects embedded NUL characters before P/Invoke for paths, prompts, JSON handoff documents, optional catalog JSON, and P2P share-kit request fields to prevent native C-string truncation at the public SDK boundary.
  - NuGet empty-string native bridge preservation on 2026-07-06: the .NET bridge marshals empty managed strings as native empty strings rather than null pointers, preserving empty prompts while reserving null for omitted optional native arguments.
  - NuGet managed share-kit request validation on 2026-07-06: the .NET P2P wrapper validates `PrepareShareKitRequest` before native JSON serialization, requiring `ModelPath` and `OutputDir` and limiting `PieceSize` to 1 KiB through 16 MiB while Rust keeps deeper URL, identifier, manifest, and artifact validation.
  - NuGet managed P2P JSON budget validation on 2026-07-06: the .NET P2P wrapper mirrors Rust P2P JSON byte budgets before P/Invoke, rejecting manifests over 1 MiB, announcements or local import receipts over 256 KiB, and announcement catalogs over 4 MiB as managed argument errors before native allocation or parsing.
  - NuGet declared package-file audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit reports now list declared package-file entries and package documentation entries, expose `missing_package_file_count`, and fail when declared README/license files are missing from `.nupkg` contents.
  - NuGet package documentation hash parity audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit reports now list expected package documentation entries with source/package SHA-256 values and fail when packaged README/license/package docs do not byte-match the current `docs/nuget` source files.
  - NuGet exact package-set audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit reports now list the expected source-versioned package names plus missing/unexpected package entries and fail if `artifacts/packages` contains anything except TinyRustLM.Abstractions, TinyRustLM.Core, and TinyRustLM.P2P at the source-declared version.
  - NuGet package identity audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit reports now record expected package ID/version for each protected `.nupkg` and fail if nuspec `id` or `version` differs from the protected filename and source-declared package version.
  - NuGet public dependency graph audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit reports now list expected dependency entries plus missing/unexpected dependency entries and fail if Abstractions gains package dependencies, Core depends on anything except same-version Abstractions, or P2P depends on anything except same-version Abstractions and Core.
  - NuGet dependency metadata policy audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit expected dependency entries now include `exclude=Build,Analyzers`, and missing/unexpected dependency checks fail if protected package references drift from that metadata policy.
  - NuGet native asset placement audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit reports now list unexpected_native_entries/unexpected_native_entry_count and fail if native runtime entries appear outside TinyRustLM.Core.
  - NuGet native asset filename audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit reports now record allowed_native_entries and fail if TinyRustLM.Core carries native files outside the approved RID/native filename set: Windows tinyrustlm_native.dll, Linux libtinyrustlm_native.so, and macOS libtinyrustlm_native.dylib.
  - NuGet package entry allow-list audit gate on 2026-07-06: package-audit reports now list package_entry_names, allowed_package_entry_patterns, and unexpected_package_content_entries, and fail if protected .nupkg contents drift outside NuGet metadata, nuspec, README/license, package docs, lib/net8.0 DLL/XML outputs, or approved Core native assets.
  - NuGet P2P URL hardening on 2026-07-06: the public SDK validates `PublicBaseUrl` directly before writing announcements, accepts only HTTPS or explicit-port loopback HTTP manifest URLs, and rejects credentials, whitespace, query strings, fragments, backslashes, dot-segment traversal, and encoded traversal before metadata is trusted.
  - NuGet P2P announcement conflict gate on 2026-07-06: the public SDK deduplicates honest announcement replays but rejects received announcements or existing catalogs where the same peer and manifest identity changes model id, manifest URL, manifest SHA-256, artifact SHA-256, or artifact byte count.
  - NuGet P2P catalog inspection gate on 2026-07-06: the public SDK exposes typed `P2PAnnouncementCatalogInspection` plus `InspectAnnouncementCatalogJson`, reports catalog SHA/count/byte evidence, and rejects catalog JSON above 4 MiB before parsing or applying received announcements.
  - MiniModel manifest verifier hardening on 2026-07-06: signed manifests now require `signature.kind=external-signature-v0`, no comments, present `signature.key_id`, a safe `signature.public_key_route`, and an exact canonical `signature.payload_sha256` over sorted non-signature manifest fields; `minimodel verify-manifest` prints that digest, while full cryptographic key-policy and transparency-log trust remain future work.
  - NuGet public publication status on 2026-07-06: local package-folder feed-current and feed-hash verification pass for `TinyRustLM.Abstractions`, `TinyRustLM.Core`, and `TinyRustLM.P2P` version `0.1.1`, but `eng\verify-feed-current.ps1 -NuGetSource https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json -ReportOutput artifacts\reports\tinyrustlm-nuget-org-feed-current.json` reports zero listed versions for all three package IDs and `eng\audit-nuget-release-readiness.ps1` / `.sh` currently reports `blocked_missing_api_key`; do not claim public NuGet.org availability until authenticated publish and NuGet.org feed-current/feed-hash verification pass.
  - Hugging Face search rows in TinyRustLM are metadata until MiniModel metadata names an admitted .slm with peer-offer proof and a catalog-listed or user-supplied consenting peer source, or the user locally converts source bytes with Rust, verifies the .slm, and imports it through the browser file picker.
  - When Hugging Face metadata includes safe `.safetensors` sibling names, TinyRustLM may show those source-file hints in rows and local conversion scripts, but it must not download, proxy, or treat them as runnable model bytes.
