  - TinyRustLM's simple Hugging Face lane defaults P2P on, shows P2P Import only for MiniModel matches with peer-offer proof plus validated catalog peer source or saved Known peer URL, shows Set Peer URL for proof-ready rows without a known source, shows Start Conversion for normal supported `.safetensors` source rows, shows Review Conversion for large, unknown-size, or GGUF source rows, and shows one list-level warning when P2P is disabled.
  - TinyRustLM's simple P2P panel and Advanced source details can load `minimodel.peer_contact_card` JSON or `minimodel.peer_contact_book.v0` JSON, validate metadata-only direct-peer URL envelopes, embedded card SHA-256s, duplicate peer rejection, no-project-server/no-model-byte/no-peer-piece/no-catalog-claim flags, render all reviewed book peers as a chooser, set the list-level Known peer URL from the selected reviewed peer, and refresh proof-ready rows to P2P Import without fetching model bytes; root-package `hf-peer-contact-card-ui` / `hf-peer-contact-book-ui` smokes prove that path, and paired reject smokes prove unsafe metadata fails closed without peer import downloads.
  - TinyRustLM's Local Connect Approvals drawer stores a local-only `tinyrustlm.local_connect_approval_policy.v0` `policy_version=2` policy with `Ask every time`, `Always approve selected`, `Trust Browsers + Email`, and high-risk `Full local-control lab mode` gated by `full_control_non_sensitive_machine_acknowledged`; browser/email/docs/files/terminal/secrets categories carry visible risk warnings, approved app names stay in local storage with explicit `approved_app_bindings`, the browser can export `tinyrustlm-local-connect-policy.v0.json`, endpoint app rows expose approve-app/approve-category/block-category controls, disable app-level approval for terminal/password categories, and recompute decisions immediately when acknowledged full lab mode is selected, `local-connect-approval-ui` proves the policy UI without touching Hugging Face or MiniModel metadata routes, and the Rust `tinyrustlm-local-connect` gate validates policy JSON plus bounded name-only `/v0/apps` rows, rejects binding drift and critical-category app-level approvals, and returns category-bound `allow`/`ask`/`deny` endpoint decisions before action execution. The current `serve-approval-endpoint` loopback API exposes health/categories/apps/decision/action routes, revalidates the watched policy file before each request, applies valid saved-policy replacements without restart, returns `policy-reload-failed` instead of stale approvals when the watched policy is invalid, can mark known app rows as `Found locally` without returning executable paths, makes `/v0/decision` and `/v0/action` category-bound for approved app names, makes `/v0/action` digest-bound and dry-run-by-default, limits execution to typed native-opener actions, and is exercised through browser-smoke `local-connect-rust-endpoint-ui`.
  - Peer URL, peer contact card/book, and P2P toggle refreshes preserve accepted Hugging Face `.safetensors` source metadata, so `Start Conversion` / `Review Conversion` fallbacks remain available after a P2P Import handoff; the source `hf-p2p-import-kit-exec` browser smoke now verifies the conversion-kit-to-peer-import path, local browser import of the peer-assembled `.slm`, and Rust/WASM generation end to end.
